%LC理
\dAsami...!\d%K%P
「麻实…」%K%P
As Asami squeezed my hand back and leaned against the wall\nnext to me -- resting her head on my shoulder -- her usual\nfragrance began to fill my nostrils.%K%P
我们一起倚靠在墙边，她紧紧地反握住我的手，\n依偎在我的肩头，传来了一如往常的味道。%K%P
I could feel the characteristically soothing scent of her\nhair and body surround me.%K%P
麻实的发香与身体味道，让我感到安心…%K%P
...%K%P
………%K%P
%LCAsami
%LC麻实
\dIt was about half a year after we separated when I found\nout.\d%K%P
「我是在分手前的半年前知道的」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\d...\d%K%P
「………」%K%P
%LCAsami
%LC麻实
\dI started feeling a little sick one day and thought it\nmight have finally been you-know-what, so I went to a\ngynecologist straight away, hoping for good news.\d%K%P
「我的身体有些异样，感觉会不会是有了，\n于是就满怀期待地去了妇产科」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dSo, that was when...\d%K%P
「那是，那时候…」%K%P
Back when Asami had mentioned to me that she might be\npregnant...?%K%P
麻实第一次对我说，『或许有了』的那时候…%K%P
%LCAsami
%LC麻实
\dI really shouldn't have gotten so ahead of myself back\nthen. I shouldn't have said anything before I went to see\na doctor first...\d%K%P
「那个时候操之过急，真是不好意思。\n现在想来，等检查完毕后再下判断才是对的…」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dThat doesn't matter now.\d%K%P
「那，不是吧」%K%P
Two and a half years since we started living together.\nA year and a half since we married.%K%P
开始住在一起，两年半。\n结为连理，一年半。%K%P
Finally... Belatedly... At long last...%K%P
『接着』，『终于』，『渐渐』…%K%P
I was prepared and ready for my incredibly busy life to\ntake a dramatic turn.%K%P
每天忙得一塌糊涂的日常生活，\n发生了戏剧性的变化，我并不是没有心理准备。%K%P
%LCAsami
%LC麻实
\dBut I was really happy about the possible news myself, so\nI just couldn't keep it to myself.\d%K%P
「可是我啊，觉得『这次』是真有了。\n一个人没忍住就说出来了…」%K%P
Despite agreeing to have a child as soon as we got\nmarried, Asami did not get pregnant in the two years we\nspent together.%K%P
最初，约定要生育儿女的我们，\n在结婚之后的二年里，一次都没有采取避孕措施。%K%P
One month passed... two months passed... half a year\npassed... The ecstatic, newlywed atmosphere slowly\ndissipated, but we simply interpreted that as us beginning\nto mature as people.%K%P
过了一个月，两个月，半年…\n逐渐过了新婚燕尔，\n可是，我们把这些，理解为了夫妻之间的成熟。%K%P
I might have secretly wished for it to happen sooner, but\nI was still in the mood of \dit'll happen sooner or later,\nanyway.\d%K%P
虽然没有想过『现在立刻』，\n但总是觉得『嘛，总有一天』，心态非常乐观。%K%P
%LCAsami
%LC麻实
\dAfter an examination, they told me I wasn't pregnant.\nYet, for whatever reason, they still wanted me to undergo\nmore tests.\d%K%P
「检查的结果，并没有怀孕。\n但不知是何故，一直去检查，检查」%K%P
That was a whole year into our marriage... After our\nwedding anniversary had become a thing of the past...%K%P
过了一年…\n到了我们第一个结婚纪念日…%K%P
%LCAsami
%LC麻实
\dThey said there was a possibility I might be infertile.\d%K%P
「我怀疑患了不孕症…」%K%P
The subject had gradually become a taboo between us.%K%P
这个话题在我们之间，渐渐地成为了一个禁忌。%K%P
%LCAsami
%LC麻实
\dAt first, I wasn't planning to hide it. We usually never\nkept secrets from each other, and while we might not have\nbeen overly passionate, we were always on good terms.\d%K%P
「最初呢，我并没有想要隐瞒。\n对我们来说，彼此之间没有什么秘密可言，\n那时的感情不至于称为深爱，也从没有产生分道扬镳的想法」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dThat's just a given, isn't it?\d%K%P
「那当然了」%K%P
With me constantly doing overtime and going to work even\non weekends, we didn't have much time to just sit down and\ntalk.%K%P
对话渐渐地减少了。\n加班，假日加班，\n二人在一起的时间，渐渐地越来越少。%K%P
But we didn't have many fights, and once we were in each\nother's embrace, we'd stay locked together until morning.%K%P
但是我们，还是相敬如宾，\n早晨出门的时候，还是会拥抱在一起。%K%P
%LCAsami
%LC麻实
\dBesides, I was the one who insisted that we needed a\nchild. I felt like you would accept the truth without\ngetting too depressed.\d%K%P
「而且，原先说想要孩子的，是我。\n理，或许对我信誓旦旦的承诺，失望透顶了吧」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\d...\d%K%P
「………」%K%P
%LCAsami
%LC麻实
\d...But I underestimated it.\nMy offer raised your expectations too much.\d%K%P
「…嗯，果然还是太天真了。\n理，果然是对我怀抱着太大的期待呢」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dThat's not true...\d%K%P
「那种事…」%K%P
%LCAsami
%LC麻实
\dAfter hearing you talk about it with your mother over the\nphone, and seeing your reaction when I told you it wasn't\nit after all... I ended up being unable to break the news\nto you anymore.\d%K%P
「你给老家的婆婆打电话，\n她说到这样下去不行时的反应，\n见到如此情形，我也越来越无法将这事告诉你了…」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dYou heard that...?\d%K%P
「你听到了吗，那个…？」%K%P
I thought reporting one's impending fatherhood to one's\nmother was common practice.%K%P
『也许要有孩子了』，『也许要成为父亲了』，\n将其第一个告诉的对象，一般考虑来，那是常识范围内的人选。%K%P
Well, if you didn't take into account the circumstances of\nmy family in particular.%K%P
…但是，这是在不考虑我家庭环境的情况下。%K%P
%LCAsami
%LC麻实
\dIs your mother doing well?\nYou shouldn't fight with her too much.\d%K%P
「婆婆，还好吗？\n…不要和她吵架啊？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\d...!\d%K%P
「哎…」%K%P
I didn't call her just because I was happy.%K%P
我和母亲打电话的时候，\n本来就表现不出什么单纯的开心了。%K%P
The mother I remembered would constantly fight with my\nfather while being completely indifferent towards me. Or\nrather, she seemingly regretted even giving birth to me in\nthe first place.%K%P
我记忆中的母亲，一直与父亲吵架，对独生子毫不关心，\n不仅如此，她甚至有后悔生下我。%K%P
I had no warm memories of her to speak of. I didn't recall\nher ever scolding me -- in fact, she never even had a\nproper conversation with me my entire life.%K%P
母亲怀抱着我的记忆，温柔地教导着我的记忆，\n不仅如此，就连被她责骂的记忆，我都没有留下过。%K%P
But whenever she'd abruptly express her doubts -- not as\nworry or scorn, but as a detached observation -- over me\nraising a child, I felt a surge of emotions in my chest.%K%P
所以，在那个时候…\n当我听到她用『你真的要抚育孩子吗』这般若无其事，\n全无感情色彩包含在内的口气，发表着那般简单的感想之时。%K%P
I ended up shouting at her over the phone.%K%P
我在电话中，开始了对母亲巧舌如簧般的劝说。%K%P
\dI swear I'll raise this child!\d\n\dAnd I don't need anyone's help!\d%K%P
『绝对要用自己的力量抚育』，\n『自力更生，就算一个人也要撑下去』。%K%P
%LCAsami
%LC麻实
\dYou... changed after that day.\d%K%P
「在那之后…你，有些变了」%K%P
If I could be allowed a brief digression...%K%P
题外话…%K%P
When I called my mother half a year later and told her\nabout my breakup, all she said was \dthought so.\d Her voice\nremained devoid of worry or even scorn, uttering the words\nas a detached observation and nothing more.%K%P
半年后，得知『与麻实离婚了』这一消息的母亲，\n用同样若无其事，全无感情色彩包含在内的口气，\n扔下『果真如此』，仅此一句话。%K%P
%LCAsami
%LC麻实
\dYou grew even more passionate about your work and ended\nup getting more and more big projects. Which also came\nwith an added heap of stress and pressure.\d%K%P
「那个时候，你的事业渐入佳境，\n渐渐地担上了很多工作的重任，\n渐渐地感到了压力」%K%P
From a strictly work-related perspective, those were some\nof my best days.%K%P
那个时候，工作也抵达了巅峰期。%K%P
I was the only employee with less than five years' worth\nof experience who was allowed to manage seven to eight\nfigure sums.%K%P
进入公司还不到５年的一般职员，\n在乌烟瘴气的职场上翻云覆雨，\n对周围环境视而不见，拼命地猛干硬干。%K%P
...During that one year, before the fraudulent accounting\nhad been discovered, I was moving more money than even our\npresident.%K%P
…在那一年后，直到经理的不正行为败露，\n我在那个工作岗位上，运作着比部长的经手还要大的款项。%K%P
%LCAsami
%LC麻实
\dIt was a small enough change that others would have\nlikely never noticed, but for someone who's been living\nwith you for all those years... it hurt to see you like\nthat.\d%K%P
「虽然这是周围察觉不到的微小变化，\n但对同在一个屋檐下的人来说，真的是很心痛」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dIt's my fault...\d%K%P
「我的错…」%K%P
%LCAsami
%LC麻实
\dNo, it's mine.\d%K%P
「不不，是我的错」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dHad I only noticed it...\nHad I noticed there was something heavy weighing on your\nmind...\d%K%P
「如果我能注意到…\n至少，能察觉出麻实的烦恼…」%K%P
If she had told me, I could've accepted the truth.%K%P
得知『没有希望怀孕』这一悲报之时，\n我以为自己能平平淡淡地说出『哦，这样啊』之类的话。%K%P
But I was wrong.%K%P
但，我毫无疑问地错了。%K%P
It was wrong of me to assume that acceptance was the\ncorrect choice.%K%P
觉得『平平淡淡地回答』就对了的我，\n真的是大错特错。%K%P
Asami suffered the most in this entire thing -- she was\nthe one who kept talking about all the bright\npossibilities of our future.%K%P
对我欣喜地倾诉着未来希望的麻实，\n那时的她是最痛苦的，这一点我本来一定能想到的。%K%P
I never realized that my acceptance didn't automatically\nelicit hers.%K%P
我表示自己并没有消沉，轻轻地叹了口气，\n猜想她不会和我是同样的态度吧。%K%P
%LCAsami
%LC麻实
\dIt's impossible... There's no way you could understand.\d%K%P
「不可能的，对理来说…\n那种事是不会明白的」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dBut... But I...!\d%K%P
「但是，但是我…」%K%P
%LCAsami
%LC麻实
\dIt's precisely because you're like this that I thought we\nneeded a child. I was determined to raise it together with\nyou.\d%K%P
「正是有了那样的理，\n我才想要儿女满堂的未来。\n才下定了要一起生育儿女的决心」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dAh...\d%K%P
「啊…」%K%P
%LCAsami
%LC麻实
\dSo when I learned the truth, I knew that marked the end\nbetween us. I realized you'd never become who I wanted you\nto be. That I wouldn't be able to fulfill our promise.\d%K%P
「所以啊，我就觉得“啊啊，这可不行”了。\n我眼前的理，已经不可能成为我心目中的那个理了。\n诺言，已经无法去实现了」%K%P
I was extremely picky about my food, had trouble\nunderstanding the feelings of others... I never had much\nself-confidence when dealing with people because I lacked\nso many things.%K%P
偏食，对他人的感情反应迟钝…\n就是这样，满是为人的缺点，\n也无法强行要求他人做什么。%K%P
I couldn't even argue with Asami's decision for us to\nseparate.%K%P
对于麻实的『我们分手吧』，\n直到最后，我都无法抵抗。%K%P
%LCAsami
%LC麻实
\dBut you would have never agreed to the breakup if I told\nyou the real reason.\d%K%P
「但把真相说出来，理是不会和我分手的吧？」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dOf course I wouldn't have... It was all my fault...\d%K%P
「那当然了…因为这一切都是我的错」%K%P
%LCAsami
%LC麻实
\dInstead of living a life that was a shadow of what it\nshould have been and regretting it, I figured it would\nmake more sense to cut things short and start fresh.\d%K%P
「比起拖泥带水地做了数年夫妻而后悔，\n好聚好散，或许对我们各自的重新开始会更好一些吧」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dAsami...\d%K%P
「麻实…」%K%P
%LCAsami
%LC麻实
\dI'd been wanting to become a teacher ever since I was a\nstudent. It just so happened that the \dpupil\d I ended up\n\dtutoring\d was a single man.\d%K%P
「成为一名教师，那是我从学生时期就怀有的梦想。\n…指引的对象，只是在那个时期，变成了一个成年人而已」%K%P
Asami, who decided to spend her life on my guidance...%K%P
赌上了人生，指引着我的麻实，她…%K%P
...realized she didn't possess a vital teaching aid needed\nfor her plans, and chose to give up instead of holding me\nback.%K%P
当她察觉，为了我而要去准备的，最重要的“教材”，\n正是自己所欠缺的东西时，\n她就卸下了那个职责。%K%P
%LCAsami
%LC麻实
\dLook, you're completely blameless in this.\nI still believe that I made the right choice back then.\d%K%P
「所以，你没有必要道歉。\n直到如今，我都相信，那时的判断准确无误」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dAsami...!!\d%K%P
「麻实…」%K%P
Asami was only telling the facts.%K%P
麻实所讲的，都是事实。%K%P
Yet she said nothing about her own feelings.%K%P
自己想要继续担当这教职呢，\n还是想要转身离开…%K%P
She did not say whether or not she personally wanted to\nstay.%K%P
这样的『真相』，让我一时语塞。%K%P
%LCAsami
%LC麻实
\dWell, I never expected your life to take that much of a\nnosedive afterwards. So in that sense, I do have some\nlingering feelings of regret.\d%K%P
「恩，我是没有想到，理的心情也会低落到那种地步。\n从这一点来看，我还是有些后悔的吧？」%K%P
After we reunited... it took a couple of days for her to\nstart smiling in front of me.%K%P
『第一次重逢』那一刻。\n她看到我的脸，直到对我露出微笑的几天里。%K%P
I kept wondering what went on in her head behind that\nsmile.%K%P
麻实到底是经过了几番挣扎，\n才挤出了那一番笑脸的啊。%K%P
%LCAsami
%LC麻实
\dAh, but you're great right now... just fantastic.\nSo much so that I keep thinking about how much I want you\nto make love to me.\d%K%P
「啊，可是，如今的理很好…非常好。\n好到让我想和你肌肤相亲的程度了」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dAh... ah, uah... uah...\d%K%P
「呜…呜、呜呜…呜呜…」%K%P
%LCAsami
%LC麻实
\dYou worked so hard to raise and protect a girl who wasn't\neven your own. You're trying to build up everything I\nfailed to give you.\d%K%P
「拼命地保护着那个女孩子，养育着她，爱着她…\n我给予不了你的感情，\n你靠自己的努力在抓取着」%K%P
The touch of her hand was gentle and full of warmth.%K%P
握住的手，温柔而暖和。%K%P
It soothed me, dispelling all my pain.%K%P
她消化了我内心所有的辛酸，\n进一步激励着我。%K%P
%LCAsami
%LC麻实
\dThough you were so into it that the girl in question\nended up going in a pretty... questionable direction.\d%K%P
「都是你拼命过头了，\n女孩子都被你迷得团团转啊，是吧」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI'm sorry... for everything. I'm so sorry...\d%K%P
「抱歉…一直，直到如今一直没…抱歉」%K%P
My tears would not stop. I wouldn't try to stop them,\neither.%K%P
我的泪止不住地流了下来。%K%P
%LCAsami
%LC麻实
\dI should be the one apologizing here... for involving\nmyself in your life again.\d%K%P
「我才该说声道歉…和你再会了」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI was happy... It hurt, but it was also very nostalgic.\d%K%P
「我很开心…虽然也很难过，但真的，很怀念」%K%P
%LCAsami
%LC麻实
\dAnd I'm sorry about all the rest, too... Seems like that\nold fire ended up being rekindled on my end as well.\d%K%P
「那真是抱歉…\n有些想要破镜重圆了」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\dI was happy... I was so happy to see you hadn't\nchanged...\d%K%P
「我真的很开心…一切，都没有变…」%K%P
%LCAsami
%LC麻实
\dIt felt good, but it's too addictive.\nI think it's about time we put a stop to this.\d%K%P
「虽然很开心…虽然再次耽溺于其中了…\n但也差不多该停下了」%K%P
%LCOsamu
%LC理
\d...\d%K%P
「啊…」%K%P
Before I knew it, the party next door seemed to have\nended.%K%P
不知什么时候，旁边的喧闹声停了下来。%K%P
The day when Toko finally passed her exams. The day I'd\nbeen waiting for. The fruit of all my labors over the\ncourse of this past year.%K%P
我一直期望着的，都子合格的这一天。\n她与我一年的努力，终于有了回报的这一天…%K%P
It all ended up getting swallowed up by those two years\nfrom my past.%K%P
我的…我与麻实的两年，怀念、悔恨、伤心与幻想，\n都已经被这一天所有的喜悦与幸福完全掩盖了。%K%P
...%K%P
………%K%P
%LCKihee
%LC喜兵卫
\dAhem. It has been said since olden times that children\nare the ones who bring families together.\d%K%P
「哎～古代有个叫春日井的小孩儿…」%K%P
%LCBuntarou
%LC文太郎
\dLet's not tell that story for today, shall we, Mr.\nRetired? It's hardly an appropriate time for it anyway.\d%K%P
「老先生，您今儿个还是歇歇吧。\n这笑话也太冷了吧」%K%P
%LCYoshinori
%LC吉则
\dI wonder what those two will do...\d%K%P
「到底咋回事儿啊…那两个人」%K%P
%LCKihee
%LC喜兵卫
\dUm, which two? I can think of at least three pairings.\d%K%P
「哎，哪两个人？\n现在不是有三组人么？」%K%P
%LCBuntarou
%LC文太郎
\dKeep any jokes about the li'l landlord to yourself, okay?\nThis is her special day and everything.\d%K%P
「今天对房东小妹来说是难得的一天吧？\n算是个非常可喜可贺的日子啊」%K%P
%LCYoshinori
%LC吉则
\dLaid-off's from the sticks, isn't he? Not being able to\nhave kids sounds like one hell of an impediment.\d%K%P
「失业的原本是个乡下人。\n生不了孩子，也许还真是个很大的障碍啊」%K%P
%LCKihee
%LC喜兵卫
\dThings seemed to have been going quite swimmingly between\nthem, too. So swimmingly, in fact, that it nearly made our\nYoung Mistress lose her mind.\d%K%P
「最近感觉他们之间的气氛挺不错的。\n…但也正因为如此，小房东才感到很不舒服啊」%K%P
%LCYoshinori
%LC吉则
\dStill, choosing -her- because your partner can't have any\nchildren is a bit... out there for a thirty-year-old guy.\d%K%P
「可是，因为做不到就选了{美都子:小孩子}，\n３０岁老爷们儿的伦理观可是毁了啊」%K%P
%LCBuntarou
%LC文太郎
\dCould you guys cut it out?!\nI can't believe I'm suddenly the voice of reason in this\nroom!\d%K%P
「你们都给我适可而止吧！\n搞得我今天像是最正常的人了啊！？」%K%P
%LCKaya
%LC夏夜
\dIf it was me, I wouldn't have left him...\d%K%P
「换了我，是不会和他分手的…」%K%P
%LCHimeo
%LC姫绪
\dThen what would you have done?\d%K%P
「那你准备怎么办？」%K%P
